<title>UK: De La Rue buys Philips smart card unit.</title>
<headline>De La Rue buys Philips smart card unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's De La Rue said on Thursday it would buy a smart card unit from Philips Electronics NV for 54.2 million stg cash plus assumed debt of about 1.9 million stg.</p>
<p>The unit, Philips Cartes et Systemes SAS (PCS), is located in France and employs 370 workers.  </p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition of PCS will now provide De La Rue with full access to smart card product technology to augment the company's traditional card printing and security skills,&quot; the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>PCS had a pretax loss of 500,000 stg on sales of 30.6 million stg in 1996.</p>
<p>The deal was expected to be completed on May 23. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
